  "reciprocity_interface": "Let f_0(Q)=U(x(Q)), with divisor S+(-S)-2n[O], and let h_P(Q)=h(Q+P). For disjoint support, Weil reciprocity gives product_j f_0(T_j-P) = f_0(A-P) product_i f_0(R_i-P) times product_(Q in S union -S) h(Q+P) / h(P)^(2n). After clearing unit denominators, the identity extends by specialization to candidate-zero rows; those rows are not claimed as literal disjoint-support evaluations.",
  "schema": "p1553.m6_generalized_miller_elliptic_resultant_swap.r167.v1",
  "target_divisor_interface": "For target points T_1,...,T_N, set S_T=sum_j T_j and C=-S_T. Choose distinct auxiliary points R_1,...,R_(N-1), and set A=S_T-sum_i R_i. Degree-(N+1) functions F_num and F_den with zeros (T_1,...,T_N,C) and (A,R_1,...,R_(N-1),C) exist because each zero list sums to O. Their quotient h=F_num/F_den has divisor sum_j[T_j]-[A]-sum_i[R_i]; the shared zero C and equal poles at O cancel."
